    {
      "fileName": "revealing-stab.json",
      "id": "JHcvySfCM9uYNb9N",
      "name": "Revealing Stab",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "JHcvySfCM9uYNb9N",
        "folder": "i69cshtrOWvVMzxH",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Revealing Stab",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "action"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": 2
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You are wielding a melee weapon that can deal piercing damage.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>You drive your piercing weapon into an imperceptible foe, revealing its location to your allies. Make a Strike with a piercing melee weapon. If the target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Concealed], you don't need to attempt a flat check to target it, and if it's @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Hidden], the DC of the flat check to target it is 5. If you hit and deal damage, you can drive the weapon you attacked with into the target (if it's corporeal), revealing its current position. You Release the weapon, and it becomes lodged in the target. If the target is concealed, no flat check is needed to target it, and if it's hidden, the DC of the flat check to target it is 5, and the creature can't become undetected. These benefits apply only for observers who can see your weapon stuck in the target. If the target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Invisible], the weapon remains visible while lodged in it.</p>\n<p>This benefit lasts until the weapon is removed from the creature. An adjacent creature or the target can remove the weapon with two Interact actions.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 6
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": []
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Player Core"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "fighter"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 6,
      "category": "class"
    },
    {
      "fileName": "ricochet-stance-fighter.json",
      "id": "tRHjUCl0xqG97nok",
      "name": "Ricochet Stance (Fighter)",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "tRHjUCl0xqG97nok",
        "folder": "i69cshtrOWvVMzxH",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Ricochet Stance (Fighter)",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "action"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>You adopt a stance to rebound your thrown weapons toward you. While you are in this stance, any thrown weapons you use as part of a ranged Strike to deal bludgeoning or slashing damage immediately return to your hand, enabling you to use them for additional Strikes. You must be within the weapon's listed range increment and have a hand free to catch the weapon. If you make a ranged Strike with a thrown weapon outside of its listed range increment, it instead flies back toward you a number of feet equal to its listed range increment and then falls to the ground.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 6
          },
